    "componentBasis": "Ancillary POIs constrain the Roman and older mammisi, basilica and sanatorium. The unmeasured ordinary visitor diagram provides relative axes and approximate dimensions; ordinary photographs show a roofed Roman mammisi, roofless older mammisi/basilica/sanatorium, partially roofed Isis chamber and dry sacred lake. Isis, lake, north portal and mudbrick wall positions remain visual estimates. The archaeological tourism boundary is not used as an ancient wall survey. The precinct is an eroded tapering mudbrick circuit with a north gate opening, not a clean extrusion of the managed-site boundary. Individual damage patterns, carved portraits and hieroglyphs are not reproduced."
